---
// About: "My story". Personal, but written for people deciding whether to work with Lucas.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro'
import TitleBlock from '../components/TitleBlock.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import { site } from '../data/site'
import '../styles/pages/about.css'

import portrait from '../assets/photos/about/portrait.jpg'
import soccerTrack from '../assets/photos/about/soccer-track.jpg'
import volunteering from '../assets/photos/about/volunteering.jpg'
import photoSample from '../assets/photos/about/photography-sample.jpg'
import workbench from '../assets/photos/about/workbench.jpg'

const facts = [
  { label: 'Name', value: site.fullName },
  { label: 'School', value: site.schoolShort },
  { label: 'Program', value: site.program },
  { label: 'Class of', value: String(site.classOf) },
  { label: 'GPA', value: site.gpa },
  { label: 'Robotics', value: 'Six years, VEX and FRC' },
  { label: 'Co-op', value: 'Dell, Process Development' },
  { label: 'Sports', value: 'Soccer, track, lifting' },
  { label: 'Volunteers', value: 'FreeKicks Special Olympics' },
  { label: 'Based in', value: site.region },
]

const habits = [
  {
    title: 'Measure before you believe',
    body: 'I built a forex scanner that was supposed to call short-term moves. It looked smart. Then I backtested it: a 46% out-of-sample win rate when it needed 55.6% just to break even. Real ML models only got to about 51%. I never placed a trade. Now I try to test the thing before I get attached to it.',
  },
  {
    title: 'If it takes ten minutes to test, test it',
    body: 'On our FRC team, anything we can test in under ten minutes gets tested instead of argued about. A quick test settles things faster than a long debate, and nobody has to win the argument.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Ideas go on the board with no names',
    body: "Another FRC rule. Once an idea is on the board, it's the team's. That way nobody defends a design just because it's theirs.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Write the spec, then prove it',
    body: 'For Jarvis, my home system on six Raspberry Pis, every stage starts with a written spec and every feature needs proof: a screenshot or a test that shows it working.',
  },
]

const hobbies = ['Robotics', '3D printing', 'Photography', 'Making videos', 'Building PCs', 'Electronics', 'Music', 'Pokémon cards', 'Hunting for good deals']

const description =
  'About Lucas Bianco: a vocational engineering student and robotics captain, how he got into engineering, how he works, and what he does outside the shop.'
---
<Base title="About" description={description} type="profile">
  <PageHeader title="My story" crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }]} measure={`class of ${site.classOf}`} />

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="section about-intro">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="card about-intro-card">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Portrait of Lucas Bianco"
          class="avatar about-portrait"
          widths={[200, 400]}
          sizes="200px"
          loading="eager"
        />
        <div class="stack-md">
          <h2>Hi, I'm Lucas</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            I'm a senior at {site.school} in Franklin, MA, in the {site.program} program,
            class of {site.classOf}.
          </p>
          <p>
            I like building things that are slightly too hard for me when I start. The projects I
            stick with longest are the ones with a piece I don't know how to solve yet.
          </p>
          <p>
            Right now that means captaining a VEX team, relaunching my school's FRC team from
            nothing, running the website for a NASA HUNCH project, a co-op at Dell, and a few
            software projects at home that got bigger than I planned.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How I got into engineering</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid about-story">
        <article class="card stack-sm">
          <h3 class="card-title"><Icon name="robot" />Middle school robotics</h3>
          <p>
            It started with VEX in middle school. By the end I was leading that team, and we went to
            the VEX World Championship twice.
          </p>
          <p><span class="todo">What first got you building, and the moment you knew you wanted engineering</span></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card stack-sm">
          <h3 class="card-title"><Icon name="wrench" />A vocational school</h3>
          <p>
            Picking a vocational school with an engineering program was the next step. It meant
            CAD, shop time, and certifications in precision measurement and mechatronics alongside
            regular classes, which is closer to how I like to learn.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card stack-sm">
          <h3 class="card-title"><Icon name="briefcase" />Now</h3>
          <p>
            Six years of robotics in, I captain my high school VEX team, I'm restarting our FRC
            team, and I'm on a co-op with Dell's Process Development team, alternating weeks with
            school.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I WORK -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>Most of my habits come from being wrong about something I was sure of.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <Figure
          src={workbench}
          alt="Lucas's desk and workbench with 3D printers and tools"
          caption="Where most of it happens: desk, printers, and the pegboard wall."
          sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 34rem"
        />
        <ul class="about-habits">
          {habits.map((h) => (
            <li class="card stack-sm">
              <h3>{h.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{h.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUTSIDE OF ENGINEERING -->
  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Outside of engineering</h2>
        <p>Four years of high school soccer, three years of indoor and outdoor track, and I lift.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photo-pair">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-media">
            <Image src={soccerTrack} alt="Lucas playing soccer for his high school team" widths={[400, 700, 1000]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 34rem" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">Soccer and track</h3>
          <p class="muted small">Four seasons of high school soccer, three of track. <span class="todo">One line on what sports taught you that shows up in your engineering</span></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-media">
            <Image src={photoSample} alt="A photograph taken by Lucas" widths={[400, 700, 1000]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 34rem" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">Photography</h3>
          <p class="muted small">One of my own photos. <span class="todo">What it is, where you took it, and what camera</span></p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="about-hobbies">
        <h3>What else fills my free time</h3>
        <ul class="chips">
          {hobbies.map((h) => <li>{h}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VOLUNTEERING -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Volunteering with FreeKicks</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="card stack-md">
          <p>
            Since 2024 I've volunteered with FreeKicks, a Special Olympics soccer program in
            Franklin, MA. We teach and play soccer with kids of all abilities.
          </p>
          <p>
            It taught me to communicate differently. The way I'd explain a drill to my own team
            doesn't work for every kid.
          </p>
          <p>
            It also taught me patience and a better understanding of other people, and that
            carries over to leading a robotics team.
          </p>
          <p><span class="todo">One specific moment from FreeKicks that stuck with you</span></p>
        </div>
        <Figure
          src={volunteering}
          alt="Volunteers and players on the field at a FreeKicks soccer session, shown from behind"
          caption="A FreeKicks session in Franklin. Shot from behind on purpose: no kids' faces on this site."
          sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 34rem"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LOOKING FOR -->
  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="card about-looking stack-md">
        <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
        <p>
          Engineering internships and co-ops. I'm already on a co-op with Dell's Process
          Development team, alternating weeks with school, and I want more of that: real problems,
          real hardware, and people who know more than I do.
        </p>
        <p><span class="todo">Where you want to go next: the field, college plans in general terms, the kind of role after high school</span></p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}><Icon name="mail" />Email me</a>
          <a class="button button-outline" href={site.linkedin}><Icon name="linkedin" />LinkedIn</a>
          <a class="button button-outline" href="/experience/">Full resume</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAST FACTS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Fast facts</h2>
      </div>
      <TitleBlock items={facts} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Questions people ask me</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-faq">
        <details class="card">
          <summary>Why a vocational school?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p>
              I wanted to spend real time in a shop and on CAD, not just read about it. At
              Tri-County I get both, plus certifications that mean something outside school.
            </p>
            <p><span class="todo">Your actual reason in one or two sentences</span></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>How do you have time for all of this?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p>
              Part of the answer is that I built a system for it: Jarvis puts my day, deadlines and
              projects on a screen on my wall, so I'm not deciding what to work on every time I sit down.
            </p>
            <p><span class="todo">The honest rest of the answer, in a sentence or two</span></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>VEX or FRC?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p>
              VEX is where I learned to design, code, and lead. FRC is bigger in every way:
              bigger robot, bigger team, and you have to raise the money yourself. Starting an FRC
              team with no robot and no budget means learning how to run a team, not just a robot.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>Are you more hardware or software?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p>
              Hardware first. Robotics, CAD, and shop work come first for me. The software
              projects happen because I keep needing tools that don't exist yet.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>What's the project you're proudest of?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p><span class="todo">Pick one and say why in two sentences</span></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>What do you want to study after high school?</summary>
          <div class="about-faq-body">
            <p><span class="todo">Field of study, said in general terms (no college list)</span></p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
